Omission
- [N1] Omitted trace (input 0): i1:To initiate the process in the Pathology Department, begin with the Gross pathology request that has arrived. -> i2:After that, proceed with the Registration gross pathology request. -> i4:During the "Registration gross pathology request" step, make sure to create a barcode scan at the start. -> i3:Once the registration is complete, assign a container to the gross pathology request. -> i5:For the "Specimen description" step, pay attention to the scan start. -> i6:Then, pay attention to the scan end. -> i7:Finally, pay attention to the scan start again for the Registration gross pathology request (cont.) step. -> i8:Following that, proceed with Macroscopic description writing. Simultaneously, complete the following steps: Tissue processing, check if "Digitalization?" is required. -> i9:If the answer is "no," continue the process. -> i11:Next, check if "Digitalization?" is required again. -> i12:After that, assign cases to the pathologist and then move on to Microscopic examination and diagnosis. -> i13:Once the microscopic examination and diagnosis are complete, write the pathology report. After writing the report, confirm it. -> i14:Once the pathology report is confirmed, deliver it. Then, proceed with the post-report processing. -> i15:To conclude the pathology procedure, close it. Finally, deliver the pathology report and complete the post-report processing.
